# Walter digest (`/srv/digest`)

On-demand intelligence digests, published as https://digest.${SPARK_DOMAIN}. Covenant handles TLS and
Pocket-ID OIDC (oauth2-proxy + nginx) and proxies to `http://${BACKEND_WG_IP}:3300` over WireGuard.
Three watches: `default` (Threat Intel), `ai-security` (AI Security), `ai-research` (AI Research).

| Path | What it does |
|---|---|
| `GET /` | dashboard SPA (vanilla JS, self-hosted OFL fonts, strict CSP) |
| `GET /api/watches` | the three watches with running flag + latest run |
| `POST /api/runs/{watch}/now` | start a background run → `{"run_id": ...}` (404 unknown watch, 409 already running) |
| `GET /api/runs/{watch}` | run history, newest first |
| `GET /api/runs/{watch}/{run_id}` | `{markdown, json}` of one run (run id must be timestamp-shaped) |
| `GET /api/runs/{watch}/{run_id}/stream` | SSE progress: `collecting` → `curating` → `done` \| `error` |
| `GET /healthz` | `{"ok": true}` |

## Layout
```
compose.yaml                 app (host network, uid 10001, read-only, cap_drop ALL, tmpfs /tmp)
build/Dockerfile             python:3.13-alpine pinned by digest; deps pinned in build/requirements.txt
build/app/main.py            HTTP + run scheduling (all site values from the environment)
build/app/pipeline.py        per watch: collectors → dedupe → LLM curation → md+JSON → state (STUB until task B2)
build/app/collectors/        collect_threat_intel.py, collect_ai_digest.py (stdlib only)
build/app/static/            index.html, app.css, app.js, fonts/ (Orbitron, Inter, JetBrains Mono + OFL licenses)
secrets/digest-litellm-key   copy of /srv/gateway/keys/digest.key (root:10001 0440)
state/                       watch state files + runs/{watch}/<run_id>.{md,json} (Walter is the source of truth)
```
Back up these config files: `compose.yaml`, `build/**`, `README.md`, and `state/` (the run history and
watch cutoffs). Do not back up `secrets/`, which is re-creatable.

## How it works
- A run is a background task: `POST /api/runs/{watch}/now` returns a timestamp-shaped run id immediately,
  and `pipeline.run_watch(watch, state_dir, progress)` does the work — collectors/ fetch the sources,
  items are deduped against the watch state file (seen ids + cutoff), the LLM (LiteLLM
  `http://${BACKEND_WG_IP}:4000/v1`, model `coder`, key from `/run/secrets/digest-litellm-key`) curates
  them, and the result is persisted to `state/runs/{watch}/<run_id>.{md,json}` with the state file advanced.
- Progress is pushed to the run view over SSE; a second run of the same watch is refused with 409 until
  the first finishes.
- Host networking is used because LiteLLM listens on `${BACKEND_WG_IP}:4000` (host network) and the app
  must bind the WireGuard IP itself. The app binds `${BACKEND_WG_IP}:3300` (IP_FREEBIND, so it starts
  even before wg0 is up).
- The container is read-only with a tmpfs `/tmp`; only `state/` is writable.
- State seeding: the workstation's `~/.hermes/*-watches/*.json` state files are pushed into
  `state/` once at deploy. After that Walter is the single source of truth — WebUI and CLI runs both
  hit the same state. If chat runs on the workstation continue before the first Walter run, state can
  diverge until Walter advances from the seed (acceptable for on-demand use).

## Firewall
- ufw: `ALLOW IN on wg0 from ${EDGE_WG_IP} to ${BACKEND_WG_IP} port 3300/tcp`. This is the effective
  gate, because host-network traffic goes through INPUT.
- `/usr/local/sbin/docker-user-rules.sh`: 3300 is added to `PORTS` (WALTER-PUBLISHED), in case the app
  is ever switched to a docker-published port.
- No other source is allowed: the public edge (Covenant) is the only client, and host-originated calls
  (the CLI below) are not filtered by WALTER-PUBLISHED.

## Secrets
| secret | path | mode / owner | how |
|---|---|---|---|
| LiteLLM virtual key for digest | `/srv/digest/secrets/digest-litellm-key` | 0440 root:10001 | copied from `/srv/gateway/keys/digest.key` (created by `provision-keys.py` after `digest` is added to `HARNESS_KEYS`). The copy must happen after the gateway/provision-keys step; on rotation re-copy by hand: `sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g 10001 /srv/gateway/keys/digest.key /srv/digest/secrets/digest-litellm-key` |

## Operations
```bash
cd /srv/digest
sudo docker compose ps                 # (healthy)
sudo docker compose up -d --build      # after editing build/
sudo docker compose logs -f app

# trigger a run from the workstation (CLI path — no new firewall surface):
ssh ${BACKEND_SSH_USER}@${BACKEND_LAN_IP} 'curl -fsS -X POST http://${BACKEND_WG_IP}:3300/api/runs/default/now'
ssh ${BACKEND_SSH_USER}@${BACKEND_LAN_IP} 'curl -fsS http://${BACKEND_WG_IP}:3300/api/runs/default'
# then open the run in the web UI (passkey login on digest.${SPARK_DOMAIN}) or
# curl -fsS http://${BACKEND_WG_IP}:3300/api/runs/<watch>/<run_id>

# LiteLLM key rotated: re-copy it (read on every curation call, no restart needed)
sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g 10001 /srv/gateway/keys/digest.key secrets/digest-litellm-key
```

## Rollback
```bash
cd /srv/digest && sudo docker compose down && sudo docker image rm walter-digest:local
sudo ufw delete allow in on wg0 from ${EDGE_WG_IP} to ${BACKEND_WG_IP} port 3300 proto tcp
sudo sed -i '/3300/d' /usr/local/sbin/docker-user-rules.sh   # remove 3300 from PORTS (keep a .bak first)
sudo systemctl restart docker-user-rules.service && sudo iptables -S WALTER-PUBLISHED   # no 3300 lines
sudo rm -rf /srv/digest
```
Then remove the digest vhost and the second oauth2-proxy instance on Covenant. That is owned by the
edge agent. `state/` is kept by `compose down` (plain bind mount); remove it only if you also want to
drop the run history.
